      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "The lines $y = 2x - 12$ and $tx + 6y = 4$ are perpendicular. What is the value of $t$?$t =$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nConverting the second line to slope-intercept form gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tx+6y & =4 \\\\ 6y & =-tx+4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{t}{6}x+\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(2)\\cdot (-\\frac{t}{6})=-1\\,\u27f9\\,t=3.\n$$",
